      "properties": {
        "id": "M1435.B1",
        "mine feature category": "mine boundary",
        "mine feature subcategory": "underground",
        "data source date": "2025-07-01 00:00:00",
        "notes": "The Abayskaya mine is part of the Karaganda Coal Mines Complex that includes eight underground coal mines and the Vostochnaya coal preparation plant. These mines are: Kostenko, Kuzembaeva, Saranskaya, Abayskaya, Kazakhstanskaya, Lenina, Shakhtinskaya and Tentekskaya coal mines, https://web.archive.org/web/20250207022321/https://miningdataonline.com/property/1772/Karaganda-Coal-Mines-Complex.aspx. \n\nPages 4-5 of Appendix 1 of the public hearings in the form of open meetings on the draft Environmental Impact Assessment for the Mining Plan for the development of coal reserves at the Abayskaya mine for the period up to 2042, from 4/2021, https://web.archive.org/web/20250703133751/https://www.gov.kz/uploads/2021/4/10/b17a033400f3f948ad85772ba135a382_original.5624626.pdf,  describes the mining boundaries in terms of coal seams, together with coal field dimensions : area no. 1  4800-6000m x 1050-3000m (5-18 sq km), area no. 2  3600-4000m x 1500-2000m (5-8 sq km) - giving a total coal field dimensions range of approx 10 - 26 sq km.\n\nTwo adjacent mining contract boundaries for Abayskaya mine can be found using the Unified Platform for Subsoil Use, Ministry of Industry and Construction of the Republic of Kazakhstan https://web.archive.org/web/2/https://minerals.e-qazyna.kz/en/contracts-map , both of which are described as object 144, issued May 12 1997, of work type 'contracts mountain'. The northern contracts boundary is used here because it has an approximate area of 21 sq km which is within the coal field's approximate dimensions of 10 - 26 sq km given in the Appendix 1 reference above.\n\n",
        "description": "Abayskaya coal mine boundary",
